Wallace the Tourist was only the second Tourist of that name to be played.
I've played a lot of tourists that died young over the years though.  I
decided to play Tourists after seeing the First YAAP in 3.4.2 and the
comment about the new missile system.  Thanks to David Corbett for the tip
and the good Karma.



It was an atypical ascension for me, I didn't get an early /oW.  Got a Magic
Lamp somewhere after finding the quest portal (big room) and used it on a
SDSM.



My decisions. no wishing for artifacts, (A first for my ascenders) no poly
(I don't do it too often anyway)  No E-word, No murder, No dancing. (nurse
or succubus)  I added Genoless later.



I descended through to level 4 converting two lawful altars along the way.
I set up my bas of operations on level 4, the altar was near the far corner
of a large room.  Here I was gifted with Mojo.  Great place to change armor.
I dropped to level 7 and did sokoban, it yielded the BoH.  I then went back
to level 3 for the mines.  Only one unlighted level, and that was below
minetown, after I had  bought a lamp from Itzchak, noting that he only had 5
candles. I found a "oMB in the mines, the minesend was the maze, got a flint
and the luckstone.  No touchstone and damn few ?oID, so no gems this time.
I spent a long time wearing some assorted armor, never found speed boots,
and no gloves other than leather, I did find a +0 HoB.  The SDSM replaced a
+1 dwarvish mithril.  Back to the stash for more sac'ing and a water prayer.
Got Vorpy and never set it aside.  I got a CoMR and a MM from the bones of a
W, lots of assorted rings as well from three other bonesfiles.  Sometime
before the quest I killed a tengu, tucked in and got. Teleportitis!?!  I
Spent some marker charges and holy water trying to get a full ID eventually
the 5th scroll id'ed my ring collection.  No =oTC.  I had a run-in with the
Kops thanks to a random teleport.  I paid off the shopkeeper like a good
tourist and the Kops went away. (I'd see more of them on the quest.)



I did medusa with a !oLev and my trusty blindfold.  (the right side island
medusa map)  Perseaus had both the bag and boots.  I used his boots on the
next level to go around back.  Another !oLev (I had 3) got me over the
trapdoors.  A long fight in the throneroom back door, many beheadings.  I
have a new respect for Vorpy.  The castle wand was 0:2, I had a ?oCharging,
which I blessed.  Blessed +0 (wanted +3) Speed Boots,  and 3 tins of tengu
meat.  Three tins later, no TC!  I then re-charged and wished for +3 GoP and
3 c?oGeno (got one)  4 tengu corpses and still no TC.  I was glad for my
"oMB, saved me from choking. I used my marker to make some more ?EW and ?EA,
enchanted Vorpy to +7 and most of my armor (The Shirt was last, after the
quest and a PYEC recharged MM)



I had a run-in with a MF at this point, got sucked for the first and only
time, had to re-map the dungeon.  I decided to go Genoless.



On to the quest.  This was my first time through the T quest, interesting.
the shops yielded more rings. still no TC.  A Kop Captain provided a Silver
Saber which I enchanted up thanks to a marker from a shop on the quest
endlevel.  I practiced saber to skilled on the Kops.  I had longsword at
basic and started twoweaponing at this point.  The master thief was a
pushover with Twoweapon at expert.



Back to the main dungeon and down to the Valley.  I played with a /oUT on
some of the human corpses and ended up with a peaceful tourist wandering the
VotD .  Trippy.



The major demons were straightforeward, Orcus used three death rays on me,
but none even got reflected.  The PYEC and many /oDigging made the paths
easy.  I also mapped several levels using my ?oMM.  The stairs to Vlad's
tower were on the Wizard's tower level.  I had a run-in with a MMF at this
point, but I had some notice (the PYEC's telepathy) so it ate /oD.



I found the VS on level 50 after much searching.  More than I had to, thanks
to the damn Teleportitis.  I need to borrow a book.  Back up, hit a MMF in
Rodney's Zoo another charge from Orcus' wand.  I used the PYEC to recharge
it before opening the tower.  Rodney didn't want to loan me the book, so I
used a death ray to convince him.  I tinned his corpse.



Back to the VS, one wish for Candles, and wrest the last one after ID'ing
all my remaining rings without finding TC.  No way I'm doing the ascension
run with uncontrolled teleportitis.  I used Conflict in the sanctum, had
very little trouble with the priests.  A disenchanter managed to take 1 off
both of my weapons before I started using Orcus' toy on them.  Thanks to the
PYEC, I used almost as many death rays as my W ascension.  I showed Moloch's
high priest orcus' wand.  Picked up and named the Amulet c!oGL and I was
back out of the sanctum.



The mysterious force hit seven times, I was wearing TC, so I was able to get
around fairly well.  Rodney put in a few appearances along the way.  He
summoned 2 Jabberwocks at one point.  Ha!  Did I mention I liked vorpy this
game?



Rodney showed up twice on earth, double troubling for the first and only
time.  Took four shots from the wand to get them both (the 4th got them
both.)  I used Conflict on Earth, Air and Fire.  I only had 3 ?oGD so the
portal on water was found by random wandering and autosearching.  An archon
dropped demonbane shortly after entering the Astral plane.  The Guardian
Angel of the Lady mixed it up with death, after I nailed him the first time
with my twoweapon attack.  The first altar (death) was chaotic, pestilence
was guarding the lady's altar and I decided to whistle up my guardian angel
and move along to the bar.  I gave all of my gold to the High preist.



As you can see he took a few days. Avoiding YASD to Playing while
over-tired.



